  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, there is no evidence to exploit, so the priority is establishing a reference baseline that maximizes information gain for all subsequent comparisons. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest 'null' configuration in the search space: no image modality, no multiprofile aggregation, and the most straightforward RNA encoder (PCA). Establishing this baseline is critical because every other design decision—adding image data (config_010/016), switching to multiprofile (config_002/003), upgrading the RNA encoder to scVI or scGPT (config_004/007), or introducing multimodal fusion (config_016/017)—can be evaluated as a delta relative to this reference. Without it, we cannot determine whether any added complexity actually improves validation accuracy or F1. It is also the lowest-risk configuration (fewer moving parts, less chance of implementation issues), making it the most reliable first data point under a limited budget."
}

